  },
  "limits": "Vertices come from Coxeter group orbits and are capped at 3000; edges join vertices at distance 1, which is the edge length of every Wythoff polytope. Ring counts group points by radius, so two rings of h points at one radius count as one ring of 2h (the 120-cell shows 12 radii for 20 orbits). The drawing is orthographic: vertices may coincide in the plane for some ringings.",
